===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|dove}}, {{m|enm|douve}}, {{m|enm|duve}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*dūfe||dove, pigeon}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*dūbā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*dūbǭ||dove, pigeon}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|doo}}, {{m|sco|dow}}, {{cog|stq|Duuwe}}, {{cog|fy|do}}, {{cog|nl|duif}}, {{cog|af|duif}}, {{cog|srn|doifi}}, {{cog|de|Taube}}, {{cog|nds-de|Duuv}}, {{cog|nds-nl|duve}}, {{m|nds-nl|doeve}}, {{cog|da|due}}, {{cog|fo|dúgva}}, {{cog|is|dúfa}}, {{cog|nb|due}}, {{cog|nn|due}}, {{cog|sv|duva}}, {{cog|yi|טויב}}, {{cog|got|*𐌳𐌿𐌱𐍉}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/dʌv/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌv|s=1}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-dove-noun.ogg|a=US|pos=noun}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[pigeon]], especially one smaller in size and white-colored; a bird (often arbitrarily called either a [[pigeon]] or a dove or both) of more than 300 species of the family {{taxfmt|Columbidae|family}}.
# {{lb|en|countable|politics}} A person favouring [[conciliation]] and [[negotiation]] rather than [[conflict]].
#: {{syn|en|peace dove}}
#: {{ant|en|hawk}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} {{non-gloss|Term of endearment for one regarded as pure and gentle.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Song of Solomon|2|14|passage=O my '''dove''', {{...}} let me hear thy voice.}}
# A greyish, bluish, pinkish colour like that of the bird.
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} {{short for|en|love dove||tablet of the drug ecstasy}}

